  note         = {In 10 POTS women vs 11 healthy controls during 2-hour standing, the menstrual cycle modulated RAAS and hemodynamics in POTS. Cardiac output/stroke volume lower and total peripheral resistance greater in early follicular than mid-luteal phase; plasma renin and aldosterone lower in early follicular; presyncope rate greater in early follicular phase. Higher estrogen/progesterone in mid-luteal associated with more RAAS/volume retention, improving late-standing tolerance. Supports luteal-phase protection in POTS orthostatic tolerance.},
