  keywords     = {hyperparathyroidism, fibromyalgia, calcium, parathyroid hormone, misdiagnosis, differential diagnosis},
  note         = {Cross-sectional study: 100 women with fibromyalgia vs 57 healthy women. Hypercalcemic hyperparathyroidism in 6% of FM patients; 17% showed isolated high PTH (normocalcemic hyperparathyroidism), frequencies higher than expected for age. PTH significantly higher in FM (57.06 +/- 68.98 pg/mL) vs controls (37.12 +/- 19.02 pg/mL; p=0.001). No association between hyperparathyroidism and FM symptoms except epigastric pain (p=0.012). Authors ask whether these are misdiagnosed hyperparathyroidism cases rather than FM. Supports the differential-diagnosis exclusion of hyperparathyroidism in fatigue/musculoskeletal syndromes.},
